  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>According to Newton&#39;s cooling law, rate of cooling is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo></math>the&nbsp;temperature of the body</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo></math>Room temperature(constant)</p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;be the proportionality constant and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;be the initial temperature.<br />Therefore,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#8747;</mo><mo>d</mo><mi>t</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Hence, the graph is exponential.</p>"
  }
